    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0104" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/1189: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-26T16:00:00+02:00">November 26,
                            1942—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1163. Informant referred to in my 1162, today<anchor n="63" xml:id="d107-f1"/>
                    says that about month ago Molotov hinted to Swedish representatives that U. S.
                    S. R. might be inclined to discuss cessation of hostilities with Finland and
                    inquired whether Sweden would act as intermediary. Informant says these efforts
                    were fruitless at that time owing to Finnish obstinacy. I have no confirmation
                    of this report from any other source.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
